{"title":"Career roadmap · Food R&D Executive","role":"Food R&D Executive","summary":"A Food R&D Executive develops, improves and validates food products, ingredients, formulations and processing methods. The role combines food chemistry, microbiology, food processing, sensory science, nutrition, packaging, shelf-life testing, quality and regulatory knowledge.","facts":{"Current degree":"B.Tech / B.E. (Bachelor of Technology / Engineering)","Course":"Food Technology"},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Food R&D Executive Roadmap"},{"type":"p","text":"A Food R&D Executive develops, improves and validates food products, ingredients, formulations and processing methods. The role combines food chemistry, microbiology, food processing, sensory science, nutrition, packaging, shelf-life testing, quality and regulatory knowledge."},{"type":"p","text":"Typical work includes new product development, formulation optimisation, prototype preparation, pilot trials, stability studies, sensory evaluation, ingredient selection, cost optimisation and scale-up support."},{"type":"note","label":"Career-route check","text":"This is a directly accessible career path for Food Technology graduates. Entry titles can include R&D Executive, R&D Trainee, Product Development Executive, Food Technologist, Product Development Associate or Process Development Executive."},{"type":"note","label":"Timeline assumption","text":"4-year B.Tech/B.E. starting in 2026 → graduation around 2030."}]},{"heading":"Career horizons","kind":"horizons","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Period","Career focus"],"rows":[[{"text":"2026–2030"},{"text":"Build food chemistry, microbiology, processing, formulation, sensory and analytical skills."}],[{"text":"2030–2035"},{"text":"Work on product development, laboratory trials, formulation and scale-up projects."}],[{"text":"2035–2040"},{"text":"Progress to Senior R&D Executive, Product Development Specialist, Innovation Scientist or R&D Project Lead."}],[{"text":"2040–2046"},{"text":"Move toward R&D Manager, Innovation Manager, Product Development Manager or Food Technology leadership."}]]}]},{"heading":"What to build each year","kind":"build","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["When","Build this","Learn from","Proof of progress","Gap it moves"],"rows":[[{"text":"Year 1 Sem 1"},{"text":"Chemistry, biology, mathematics and food science fundamentals"},{"text":"MIT OpenCourseWare","url":"https://ocw.mit.edu/"},{"text":"Food-science mini project"},{"text":"Scientific foundation"}],[{"text":"Year 1 Sem 2"},{"text":"Food chemistry and microbiology"},{"text":"NPTEL","url":"https://nptel.ac.in/"},{"text":"Food composition/microbiology report"},{"text":"Food fundamentals"}],[{"text":"Year 2 Sem 1"},{"text":"Food processing and preservation"},{"text":"NPTEL","url":"https://nptel.ac.in/"},{"text":"Processing experiment"},{"text":"Processing knowledge"}],[{"text":"Year 2 Sem 2"},{"text":"Food analysis, ingredients and formulation"},{"text":"NPTEL + laboratory work"},{"text":"Product formulation project"},{"text":"Product-development skills"}],[{"text":"Year 3 Sem 1"},{"text":"Sensory science, shelf life and packaging"},{"text":"FDA Food","url":"https://www.fda.gov/food"},{"text":"Sensory + shelf-life study"},{"text":"R&D capability"}],[{"text":"Year 3 Sem 2"},{"text":"Product optimisation, pilot trials and scale-up"},{"text":"NPTEL + industry resources"},{"text":"Prototype + pilot process"},{"text":"Industrial readiness"}],[{"text":"Year 4 Sem 1"},{"text":"Food safety, HACCP, regulatory and quality systems"},{"text":"FSSAI","url":"https://www.fssai.gov.in/"},{"text":"HACCP/product-compliance project"},{"text":"Professional readiness"}],[{"text":"Year 4 Sem 2"},{"text":"Major product-development project + internship/placement"},{"text":"NPTEL","url":"https://nptel.ac.in/"},{"text":"Market-ready prototype + technical report"},{"text":"Employability"}]]},{"type":"h","text":"Core technical subjects"},{"type":"p","text":"Prioritise:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Food Chemistry"},{"text":"Food Microbiology"},{"text":"Food Biochemistry"},{"text":"Food Processing"},{"text":"Food Preservation"},{"text":"Food Engineering"},{"text":"Food Analysis"},{"text":"Food Additives"},{"text":"Food Packaging"},{"text":"Sensory Evaluation"},{"text":"Product Development"},{"text":"Food Product Formulation"},{"text":"Dairy Technology"},{"text":"Cereal Technology"},{"text":"Meat/Fish/Poultry Technology"},{"text":"Fruit and Vegetable Processing"},{"text":"Fermentation Technology"},{"text":"Food Safety"},{"text":"HACCP"},{"text":"Food Toxicology"},{"text":"Nutrition"},{"text":"Shelf-Life Studies"},{"text":"Quality Control"},{"text":"Food Regulations"},{"text":"Food Process Engineering"}]},{"type":"h","text":"R&D-specific capabilities"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn to perform:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Ingredient screening"},{"text":"Formulation development"},{"text":"Prototype preparation"},{"text":"Bench-scale trials"},{"text":"Pilot-scale trials"},{"text":"Sensory evaluation"},{"text":"Texture analysis"},{"text":"Colour analysis"},{"text":"Moisture analysis"},{"text":"pH/acidity testing"},{"text":"Microbiological testing"},{"text":"Shelf-life studies"},{"text":"Stability testing"},{"text":"Packaging compatibility"},{"text":"Cost/formulation optimisation"},{"text":"Scale-up"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Product-development workflow"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn the complete cycle:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Consumer need","Product concept","Ingredient selection","Formulation","Prototype","Sensory testing","Laboratory testing","Shelf-life study","Pilot trial","Scale-up","Regulatory review","Commercial launch","Post-launch improvement"]},{"type":"p","text":"This workflow is more important for an R&D Executive than simply knowing food-processing theory."},{"type":"h","text":"Specialisation"},{"type":"table","header":["Lane","Core stack","Learn from","